{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787296883131497001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"subtle-brinish-fugu","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"10c4a4bd0c2aa967096cf49cab27822951ae390f9e0d661301065b959ea0e089","event_uuid":"718e6a76-1601-454c-89ef-4c94644c36e2","position":{"commit_sha":"4fc23eaf91f0c595fdf069e189601776d72f5956","position":"1787293889926202001-718e6a76-1601-454c-89ef-4c94644c36e2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e595a3439710a5bb73126ebd5313c852e48d9fa2ecfe50ac7919630631e7ffcf","event_uuid":"3829de87-1ee7-44cd-8ef5-3919719f0baf","position":{"commit_sha":"07ffd4b6c38fa146b0e271d88e599aac5a893dc4","position":"1787293902753844001-3829de87-1ee7-44cd-8ef5-3919719f0baf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bdc3794b372736a5d27e9ff3cb3889c839b1720d13bdcbc107a7a70d24bbe7d1","event_uuid":"dc90a3d0-eb60-4f45-8452-bbe7d979e5df","position":{"commit_sha":"f8071de0b65a8cbf3d57035daf1d99e979674c44","position":"1787293910493145001-dc90a3d0-eb60-4f45-8452-bbe7d979e5df"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787293889926202001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"dc90a3d0-eb60-4f45-8452-bbe7d979e5df","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8386-a512-4815-4e6b"}],"description":"## Discovered from\n\nrebar-debug on bug `smart-disloyal-naga` (8386-a512-4815-4e6b). Re-verified there by two\nmethods and by runtime observation; recorded rather than fixed, because removing it is a\npublic-dataclass change unrelated to that bug's performance fix.\n\n## Problem\n\n`SnapshotHandle._cleanup` (`src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:199`) is declared as\n`Callable[[], None] | None = None` and read only by `__exit__` (`:212-213`). **No producer\nanywhere in `src/` ever assigns it.** `grep -rn \"_cleanup\" src/` returns exactly those two\nsites; Serena agrees.\n\nConfirmed at runtime through a real `resolve_gate_handle(...)`:\n\n    handle.source=attested sha=49d6fb2e tickets_path=set\n    handle._cleanup = None\n    after __exit__: cleanup invoked? False  (entry still on disk: True)\n\nSo `SnapshotHandle.__exit__` is a permanent no-op, and `with handle:` reads — to anyone\nskimming — as though it releases something.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nIt is not a leak (the entry is a *cache*; per-review release would defeat caching, which is why\n8386 was fixed by adding reuse rather than by adding release). The cost is that it is\n**misleading dead code** on a class whose whole subject is resource lifetime, in the exact\nmodule where a reader goes to ask \"who cleans these up?\". The honest answer is \"the janitor,\nnever the handle\", and the field says otherwise.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Either the field is removed (and `__enter__`/`__exit__` kept or dropped deliberately), or\n      it is assigned by a real producer with a documented purpose.\n- [ ] If removed, `SnapshotHandle`'s docstring states that entry lifetime is the janitor's\n      responsibility and not the handle's.\n- [ ] No caller constructs `SnapshotHandle(_cleanup=...)` (verified: none does today).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py","reason":"SnapshotHandle._cleanup field and __exit__"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":4,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"9b40-2fd7-3456-4e74","ticket_type":"task","title":"Remove or wire SnapshotHandle._cleanup — no producer assigns it, so __exit__ is a no-op","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["718e6a76-1601-454c-89ef-4c94644c36e2","3829de87-1ee7-44cd-8ef5-3919719f0baf","dc90a3d0-eb60-4f45-8452-bbe7d979e5df"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787296883131497001,"uuid":"04d8a452-7235-49ba-a75c-3475dd065535"}